    "turn_text": "It's not. You're right. It's the story of 2022. It's going to continue. For the foreseeable future, neither side, neither Putin nor Zelensky, neither the Russians, the nationalist Russians, nor almost all Ukrainians, They don't want to quit. The Ukrainians are fighting for their lives. And so they're entrenched in their views. President Zelensky has said he's not negotiating to give away Ukrainian territory. I don't think he has the political room to do that, even if he wanted to. He wouldn't be president of Ukraine anymore. It's one of the catastrophic failures of Russia, of Putin's invasion, aggressive war against Ukraine. He's driven those Slavic sisters and brothers in Ukraine that he says that Putin says are part of this Rusky mirror, this Russian world. He's driven them so far away and against Russia. And then Putin himself He doesn't want an off-ramp. I used to joke with people who always ask me, you know, what's the off-ramp",
